-- title:
--   The white noise sample space $\Omega=\mathcal S'$
-- statement:
--   $\Omega=\mathcal S'$ is the space of real continuous linear functionals on the real Schwartz space $\mathcal S(\mathbb R)$, with the σ-algebra generated by the evaluations $\omega\mapsto\langle\omega,s\rangle$, $s\in\mathcal S$.
--
--   The white noise measure $P$ lives on this space, and the white noise space is $\mathcal W=L^2(\Omega,\mathcal F,dP)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper uses the Borel σ-algebra of $\mathcal S'$; for this nuclear space it coincides with the cylinder σ-algebra of the evaluations used here. The module also declares that σ-algebra as an instance.
-- source:
--   Alpay, Jorgensen, Levanony, A class of Gaussian processes with fractional spectral measures, arXiv:1009.0233v1, §4, p.10

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory Complex Filter Topology ProbabilityTheory
open scoped SchwartzMap ENNReal

namespace FractionalSpectralGP

/-- The sample space `Ω = 𝒮'` of white noise (Alpay, Jorgensen, Levanony, arXiv:1009.0233v1, §4, p.10): the real
continuous linear functionals on the real Schwartz space `𝒮(ℝ)`, with the σ-algebra generated by
the evaluations `ω ↦ ⟨ω, s⟩`, `s ∈ 𝒮`.

**Formalization Note.** The paper takes the Borel σ-algebra of `𝒮'`; for the nuclear space `𝒮'`
this is the cylinder σ-algebra generated by the evaluations, which is the one used here. -/
abbrev Omega : Type := 𝓢(ℝ, ℝ) →L[ℝ] ℝ

/-- The evaluation (cylinder) σ-algebra on `Ω = 𝒮'`. -/
noncomputable instance : MeasurableSpace Omega :=
  ⨆ s : 𝓢(ℝ, ℝ), MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω : Omega => ω s) inferInstance

end FractionalSpectralGP


